  "placementWhy": "Similarity fit through Jailhouse (Open Caves on-site GPS, the JAILHOUSE CENOTE ENTRANCE pond on the map) and Dead Cenote (its pond, clearly visible on the satellite imagery at 20.19046, -87.49359): 0.1109 m/px, rotation +0.2 deg. Checks: the scale bar gives 0.1116 m/px (0.6% off); the printed true-north star sits 5.7 deg west of the magnetic arrow, but a placement with it puts Dead Cenote ~20 m off its pond, so it is not used. Against the placed Naranjal stick plot (the earlier fit of this map onto it, scratchpad nar/mkpar.json): 4-20 m apart over the whole map (12 m at Jailhouse, 15 m at Dead Cenote). The 'To Cenote of the Sun 131 m' arrow lands 25 m from mayan-blue's 'To Muknal' pointer; the Sixth Cenote end is 144 m from the database Cenote of the Sun (QRSS position, validity unknown) and 106 m from OSM's. The printed position (N20.18832 W087.48985) is 33 m from Jailhouse's on-site GPS."
